{"title":"Nonagon","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>A <b>nonagon</b> is a polygon with nine sides.\nA regular nonagon has equal sides and angles, with each interior angle measuring <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6afaf5934b1292780cf950d6e6ddbd98865f369e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$140^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" /> and having an angle sum of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c3756cfeb099306f0436cf4b1949eaab8c40b582.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1260^{\\circ}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Nonagon&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Polygon\" title=\"Polygon\">Polygon</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Geometry\" title=\"Geometry\">Geometry</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Nonagon&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018101442\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.009 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.014 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 19/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 262/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 363/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.284      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.284      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- 